<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Shutong Wu
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><span id="id1" class="ltx_text">Department of Computer Sciences, University of Wisconsin – Madison</span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Jiawei Zhang
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><span id="id2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{swu494, jzhang2924}@wisc.edu</span>
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Diffusion Large Language Models (DLLMs) have emerged as a new paradigm of language modeling beyond autoregressive next-token prediction. Thanks to their bidirectional attention mechanism, DLLMs are more capable of capturing the connection of context, and thus show unique advantages in challenges like the famous "reversal curse" or learning under data-constrained scenarios.
However, this bidirectional nature also brings an obstacle that DLLMs are not inherently compatible with KV Cache, and consequently, the inference efficiency is not competitive compared with autoregressive models. Taking advantage of their inherent capability of multi-token prediction, existing parallel decoding algorithms can speed up the DLLM inference, but at the cost of non-negligible performance degradation.
To overcome this challenge, we introduce <span id="abstract1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Free</span> <span id="abstract1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span>raft-<span id="abstract1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">a</span>nd-<span id="abstract1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ve</span>rification (<span id="abstract1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FreeDave</span>), a novel fast sampling algorithm tailored for DLLMs that achieves lossless parallel decoding. Specifically, we propose a pipeline of parallel-decoded candidate generation and verification, which is guaranteed to reproduce the same sequence generated by static sampling, without introducing extra model forward calls. By applying FreeDave, the throughput of DLLMs can be boosted up to <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.8\times</annotation></semantics></math> without performance degradation on math reasoning tasks.</span></p>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The advent of Large Language Models (LLMs) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> built on large transformers<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> and autoregressive (AR) next-token prediction has marked a revolutionary milestone on the way to artificial general intelligence. They have demonstrated an extraordinary capacity for text processing and generation, achieving near-human performance on a vast spectrum of natural language tasks. In recent years, their capabilities have been extending far beyond basic text completion, showing remarkable proficiency in highly specialized and challenging tasks. For instance, LLMs have made significant strides in mathematical reasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, which requires deep logical and symbolic understanding. Similarly, in the domain of software engineering, LLMs have shown promising achievements on code generation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, offering powerful tools to automate development tasks and improve development productivity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Diffusion Large Language Models (DLLMs)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> have emerged as a compelling new paradigm of language modeling. Inspired by their profound success in continuous data domains such as high-fidelity image and audio synthesis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, diffusion models have been adapted to the discrete domain, especially language modeling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>.
Despite their great potential, the practical application of DLLMs is hampered by a challenge that the efficiency of inference is limited due to the inherent incompatibility with KV Cache. Although specialized caching strategies<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> are proposed as a solution, the necessity of frequently refreshing the KV Cache remains a drag on the inference speed.
Parallel decoding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, while able to further speed up the inference by utilizing the capability of multi-token prediction of DLLMs, will usually bring a non-negligible degradation in the generation quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To cross this dilemma, we introduce <span id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Free</span> <span id="S1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span>raft-<span id="S1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">a</span>nd-<span id="S1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ve</span>rification (<span id="S1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FreeDave</span>), a novel fast sampling algorithm for DLLMs that achieves lossless parallel decoding.
FreeDave requires no model modification or any extra modules, and can be seamlessly incorporated with any existing efficient inference frameworks like DLLM caching<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>. Taking advantage of the inherent capability of parallel decoding of DLLMs, and inspired by speculative decoding applied on autoregressive LLMs for fast sampling<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>, we reveal that:</p>
<p id="S1.p3.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><em id="S1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Your DLLM is secretly a self-verifiable parallel decoder without extra cost.</em></p>
<p id="S1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">We prove, by both theoretical analysis and empirical evaluations, that FreeDave can substantially accelerate the inference of DLLMs without sacrificing the generation quality. Specifically, for TraDo models<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, currently the state-of-the-art DLLM family, FreeDave can boost the throughput up to <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.8\times</annotation></semantics></math>, while maintaining the performance on math reasoning benchmarks, including MATH500<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>, GSM8K<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>, and AIME2024<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.00294v1/FreeDave_pipeline.png" id="S1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/191;" width="476" height="191" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>The overview of FreeDave sampling for DLLMs. Based on the estimated distribution predicted by the DLLM at the current step, the remasking scheduler looks multiple steps ahead and returns multiple draft candidates at those timesteps. Then, at the next step, the DLLM takes those candidates as a batch of inputs in parallel and gets the estimated distribution for each candidate, which is further processed by the remasking scheduler for one more step to get a target sequence. The candidates, as well as their estimated distributions, are then accepted or rejected by matching their targets.
The generation and verification of the draft candidates can be understood as byproducts during the normal static sampling without introducing extra cost, except for a slight memory overhead from the batch forward. Empirically, with a high potential, the inference will get an appreciable speedup.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Related Work</h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Diffusion Large Language Models</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Diffusion Large Language Models (DLLMs) emerge as a new language modeling paradigm beyond autoregressive next token prediction.
Early foundational frameworks like D3PM<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite> generalize diffusion models from the continuous domain to discrete state-spaces, and a key finding was that using a special token as an absorbing state consistently yielded the best performance. This paved the way for Masked Diffusion Language Models (MDLMs)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>, with the simplification of the complex Evidence Lower Bound (ELBO) training objective into a more stable weighted mixture of masked language modeling (MLM) losses.
Recent studies on DLLMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, which scale up to billions of parameters, have been making remarkable progress on closing the performance gap with AR LLMs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Compared to AR LLMs, the bidirectional nature of DLLMs allows them to overcome challenges like the "reversal curse"<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>. Furthermore, recent studies have shown that DLLMs are significantly more data-efficient in data-constrained settings<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>.
On the other hand, the primary drawback of DLLMs remains their slower inference speed due to the inherent incompatibility with KV Cache, which also stems from their bidirectional nature.
To address this problem, strategies like Block Diffusion<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> interpolate between AR and diffusion paradigms by generating text in blocks, enabling the use of inter-block KV caching. dLLM-Cache<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> introduces an adaptive caching mechanism by exploiting the distinct redundancies in the internal features of DLLMs. Fast-dLLM<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> incorporates a novel block-wise approximate KV Cache mechanism and a confidence-aware parallel decoding strategy to further bridge this gap in inference speed with AR LLMs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Speculative Decoding</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To accelerate the inference of AR LLMs while maintaining the quality of the generation, speculative decoding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>, <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> is designed to perform multiple decoding steps in parallel with verifiable acceptance. Generally, a lightweight draft model, which is much faster than the LLM, autoregressively performs next-token prediction for multiple steps to generate multiple candidates, and then those candidates are fed to the target model, <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.</em> the LLM itself, for verification, usually by rejection sampling, to get accepted or rejected. After that, the process of candidate generation and verification is repeated, starting from the first rejected token in the last turn. However, the draft model is required to be aligned with the target models as much as possible, otherwise, the low acceptance rate of candidates will instead bring inefficiency to the LLM inference by introducing extra draft model calls while being unable to appreciably reduce the LLM calls. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. [38]</a></cite> proposed a speculative decoding algorithm that uses the LLM itself, with some layers skipped as the draft model and the full LLM as the target model, without the need for an external draft model. Those speculative decoding algorithms are specially tailored for AR LLMs. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christopher et al. [40]</a></cite> adopt speculative decoding to DLLMs, which still requires an external draft model.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Methodology</h2>

<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Preliminaries</h3>

<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Autoregressive language models</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the past years, autoregressive (AR) language modeling has been the predominant paradigm of LLMs. The joint distribution of generated tokens is modeled by</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(x)=\prod_{i=1}^{L}p_{\theta}(x^{i}|x^{&lt;i}),\hskip 10.00002ptx^{&lt;i}=\begin{cases}\{x^{j}|j=1,\dots,i-1\}&amp;\text{if }i\geq 2\\
\emptyset&amp;\text{if }i=1\end{cases}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(x)=\prod_{i=1}^{L}p_{\theta}(x^{i}|x^{&lt;i}),\hskip 10.00002ptx^{&lt;i}=\begin{cases}\{x^{j}|j=1,\dots,i-1\}&amp;\text{if }i\geq 2\\
\emptyset&amp;\text{if }i=1\end{cases},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is a response sequence of length <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the one-hot vector of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th token in the vocabulary space, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{&lt;i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{&lt;i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subsequence of all tokens before the <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th token.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Diffusion language models</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Like diffusion models on continuous spaces<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[]</cite>, DLLMs model the transition from data distribution to noise distribution on discrete spaces by a forward noising process, and generate data from noise by the corresponding reverse denoising process. Generally, the forward process diffuses the data distribution toward a uniform distribution over the discrete space, or an absorbing state, and the latter is usually adopted for language modeling<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>. Specifically, for a time level <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> evolving from 0 to 1, the forward process progressively replaces each unmasked token in the original sequence <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> independently with a special mask token <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">m</span> with an increasing probability <em id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">w.r.t.</em> <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and once a token is masked, it will remain masked till <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Eventually, at <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>, all the tokens in the sequence will be <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">m</span>. This forward process with the absorbing state <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">m</span> can be formulated as</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(x_{t}|x_{0})=\prod_{i=1}^{L}q(x_{t}^{i}|x_{0}^{i})=\prod_{i=1}^{L}\text{Cat}\left(x_{t}^{i};\alpha_{t}x_{0}^{i}+(1-\alpha_{t})\textbf{m}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">m</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(x_{t}|x_{0})=\prod_{i=1}^{L}q(x_{t}^{i}|x_{0}^{i})=\prod_{i=1}^{L}\text{Cat}\left(x_{t}^{i};\alpha_{t}x_{0}^{i}+(1-\alpha_{t})\textbf{m}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the transferred sequence at the time level <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the noising schedule monotonically decreasing <em id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">w.r.t.</em> <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfies <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and Cat represents the categorical distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The reverse process is induced to progressively recover the original sequence from an all-mask sequence at <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, the reverse process transferring the sequence <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at a time level <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to the sequence <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> at an earlier time level <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq s&lt;t\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq s&lt;t\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>) can be formulated as</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(x_{s}|x_{t},x_{0})=\prod_{i=1}^{L}q(x^{i}_{s}|x^{i}_{t},x^{i}_{0})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(x_{s}|x_{t},x_{0})=\prod_{i=1}^{L}q(x^{i}_{s}|x^{i}_{t},x^{i}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(x^{i}_{s}|x^{i}_{t},x^{i}_{0})=\begin{cases}\text{Cat}(x^{i}_{s};x^{i}_{t})&amp;\text{if }x^{i}_{t}=\textbf{m}\\
\text{Cat}(x^{i}_{s};\frac{(1-\alpha_{t})\textbf{m}+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t})x^{i}_{0}}{1-\alpha_{t}})&amp;\text{if }x^{i}_{t}\neq\textbf{m}\\
\end{cases}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">m</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">m</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">m</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(x^{i}_{s}|x^{i}_{t},x^{i}_{0})=\begin{cases}\text{Cat}(x^{i}_{s};x^{i}_{t})&amp;\text{if }x^{i}_{t}=\textbf{m}\\
\text{Cat}(x^{i}_{s};\frac{(1-\alpha_{t})\textbf{m}+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t})x^{i}_{0}}{1-\alpha_{t}})&amp;\text{if }x^{i}_{t}\neq\textbf{m}\\
\end{cases},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and once a token is unmasked, it will remain unchanged till <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. If we train a parameterized model <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\cdot,\cdot):\mathbb{R}^{L\times|V|}\times\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{L\times|V|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\cdot,\cdot):\mathbb{R}^{L\times|V|}\times\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{L\times|V|}</annotation></semantics></math> to estimate the distribution of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(x_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(x_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math>, given the sequence <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at time level <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the reverse process can be formulated as</p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta}(x^{i}_{s}|x^{i}_{t})=q(x^{i}_{s}|x^{i}_{t},x^{i}_{0}=f_{\theta}(x^{i}_{t},t))=\begin{cases}\text{Cat}(x^{i}_{s};x^{i}_{t})&amp;\text{if }x^{i}_{t}=\textbf{m}\\
\text{Cat}(x^{i}_{s};\frac{(1-\alpha_{t})\textbf{m}+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t})f^{i}_{\theta}(x_{t},t)}{1-\alpha_{t}})&amp;\text{if }x^{i}_{t}\neq\textbf{m}\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">m</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">m</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">m</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta}(x^{i}_{s}|x^{i}_{t})=q(x^{i}_{s}|x^{i}_{t},x^{i}_{0}=f_{\theta}(x^{i}_{t},t))=\begin{cases}\text{Cat}(x^{i}_{s};x^{i}_{t})&amp;\text{if }x^{i}_{t}=\textbf{m}\\
\text{Cat}(x^{i}_{s};\frac{(1-\alpha_{t})\textbf{m}+(\alpha_{s}-\alpha_{t})f^{i}_{\theta}(x_{t},t)}{1-\alpha_{t}})&amp;\text{if }x^{i}_{t}\neq\textbf{m}\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta}(x_{s}|x_{t})=\prod_{i=1}^{L}p_{\theta}(x^{i}_{s}|x^{i}_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta}(x_{s}|x_{t})=\prod_{i=1}^{L}p_{\theta}(x^{i}_{s}|x^{i}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Generally, for better generation quality, the transition from <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is not by directly sampling <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(x_{s}|x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(x_{s}|x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Instead, we have a remasking scheduler <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> (usually rule-based and unparameterized)
to decide which <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">m</span> tokens to be transferred to unmasked tokens at the current time level.
<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
                
                
                
              Empirically, greedily unmasking positions with the highest-confidence unmasked tokens usually yields good quality of generation. Unless specified, in this paper, we focus on the greedy remasking scheduler.</span></span></span>
The remasking scheduler <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> takes as input a source time level <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, a target time level <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, and the estimated distribution of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> at the source time level <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (<em id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.</em> <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(x_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(x_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> here), and returns a decision set <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t\rightarrow s}=\{(a_{1},z_{1}),\dots,(a_{n},z_{n})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t\rightarrow s}=\{(a_{1},z_{1}),\dots,(a_{n},z_{n})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where in each tuple <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the transferred index and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{j}\sim\text{Cat}(f^{a_{j}}_{\theta}(x_{t},t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{j}\sim\text{Cat}(f^{a_{j}}_{\theta}(x_{t},t))</annotation></semantics></math> is the transferring target token sampled from the estimated distribution. Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Diffusion language models ‣ 3.1 Preliminaries ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> demonstrates the whole sampling pipeline by the reverse process with model <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> DLLM Static Sampling</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              Model <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, remasking scheduler <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, total generation length <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, total sampling steps <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, time schedule array <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{T}=\{t_{0},\dots,t_{N}|1=t_{0}&gt;t_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;t_{N-1}&gt;t_{N}=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐓</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{T}=\{t_{0},\dots,t_{N}|1=t_{0}&gt;t_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;t_{N-1}&gt;t_{N}=0\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              The generated sequence <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{t_{0}}\leftarrow\textbf{m}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">m</mtext><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{0}}\leftarrow\textbf{m}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0:N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0:N-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}_{0}\leftarrow f_{\theta}(x_{t_{i}},t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}_{0}\leftarrow f_{\theta}(x_{t_{i}},t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t_{i}\rightarrow t_{i+1}}\leftarrow g(\tilde{x}_{0},t_{i},t_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t_{i}\rightarrow t_{i+1}}\leftarrow g(\tilde{x}_{0},t_{i},t_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> decision returned by the remasking scheduler
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t_{i+1}}\leftarrow x_{t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{i+1}}\leftarrow x_{t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{j},z_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{j},z_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t_{i}\rightarrow t_{i+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t_{i}\rightarrow t_{i+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{a_{j}}_{t_{i+1}}\leftarrow z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{a_{j}}_{t_{i+1}}\leftarrow z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> replace masked tokens according to the decision
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leftarrow x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leftarrow x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Free Draft-and-Verification Sampling</h3>

<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Sampling Path and Oracle Path)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the reverse process of DLLM <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, a sampling path of <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> steps following a time schedule array <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[t_{0},\dots,t_{N}|1=t_{0}&gt;t_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;t_{N-1}&gt;t_{N}=0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{0},\dots,t_{N}|1=t_{0}&gt;t_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;t_{N-1}&gt;t_{N}=0]</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{0}\rightarrow t_{1}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{N-1}\rightarrow t_{N}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{0}\rightarrow t_{1}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{N-1}\rightarrow t_{N}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t_{i}\rightarrow t_{i+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t_{i}\rightarrow t_{i+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the decision set given at time step <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a remasking scheduler <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and a predefined time schedule array <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{T}=[t_{0},\dots,t_{N}|1=t_{0}&gt;t_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;t_{N-1}&gt;t_{N}=0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐓</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{T}=[t_{0},\dots,t_{N}|1=t_{0}&gt;t_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;t_{N-1}&gt;t_{N}=0]</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the oracle path as <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{oracle}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{0}\rightarrow t_{1}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{N-1}\rightarrow t_{N}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{oracle}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{0}\rightarrow t_{1}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{N-1}\rightarrow t_{N}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t_{i}\rightarrow t_{i+1}}=g(f_{\theta}(x_{t_{i}},t_{i}),t_{i},t_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t_{i}\rightarrow t_{i+1}}=g(f_{\theta}(x_{t_{i}},t_{i}),t_{i},t_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math> is the decision set returned by the remasking scheduler <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> at time step <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Feasible Path, Feasible Space, and Optimal Path)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the reverse process of DLLM <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, given a remasking scheduler <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and a predefined time schedule array <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{T}=[t_{0},\dots,t_{N}|1=t_{0}&gt;t_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;t_{N-1}&gt;t_{N}=0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐓</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{T}=[t_{0},\dots,t_{N}|1=t_{0}&gt;t_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;t_{N-1}&gt;t_{N}=0]</annotation></semantics></math>, if we can find a <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>-step subarray <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[t_{a_{0}},\dots,t_{a_{M}}|0=a_{0}&lt;a_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;a_{M-1}&lt;a_{M}=N,a_{i}\in\{0,\dots,N\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{a_{0}},\dots,t_{a_{M}}|0=a_{0}&lt;a_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;a_{M-1}&lt;a_{M}=N,a_{i}\in\{0,\dots,N\}]</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{i}}\rightarrow t_{a_{i+1}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{i}}\rightarrow t_{a_{i+1}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g(f_{\theta}(x_{t_{a_{i}}},t_{a_{i}}),t_{a_{i}},t_{a_{i+1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g(f_{\theta}(x_{t_{a_{i}}},t_{a_{i}}),t_{a_{i}},t_{a_{i+1}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g(f_{\theta}(x_{t_{a_{i}}},t_{a_{i}}),t_{a_{i}},t_{a_{i}+1})\cup...\cup g(f_{\theta}(x_{t_{a_{i+1}-1}},t_{a_{i+1}-1}),t_{a_{i+1}-1},t_{a_{i+1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g(f_{\theta}(x_{t_{a_{i}}},t_{a_{i}}),t_{a_{i}},t_{a_{i}+1})\cup...\cup g(f_{\theta}(x_{t_{a_{i+1}-1}},t_{a_{i+1}-1}),t_{a_{i+1}-1},t_{a_{i+1}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{i}}\rightarrow t_{a_{i}+1}}\cup\dots\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{i+1}-1}\rightarrow t_{a_{i+1}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{i}}\rightarrow t_{a_{i}+1}}\cup\dots\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{i+1}-1}\rightarrow t_{a_{i+1}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall i\in\{0,\dots,M-1\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall i\in\{0,\dots,M-1\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then the sampling path <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{0}}\rightarrow t_{a_{1}}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{M-1}}\rightarrow t_{a_{M}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{0}}\rightarrow t_{a_{1}}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{M-1}}\rightarrow t_{a_{M}}}]</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as a feasible path. And consequently, we define <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(f_{\theta},g,\mathbf{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐓</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(f_{\theta},g,\mathbf{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, which consists of all possible feasible paths, as the feasible space.
There exists an optimal path <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}^{\star}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{a^{\star}_{0}}\rightarrow t_{a^{\star}_{1}}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{a^{\star}_{M-1}}\rightarrow t_{a^{\star}_{M}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}^{\star}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{a^{\star}_{0}}\rightarrow t_{a^{\star}_{1}}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{a^{\star}_{M-1}}\rightarrow t_{a^{\star}_{M}}}]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbf{p}^{\star}|\leq|\mathbf{p}|\leq|\mathbf{p}_{oracle}|,\forall\mathbf{p}\in\mathcal{P}(f_{\theta},g,\mathbf{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐓</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{p}^{\star}|\leq|\mathbf{p}|\leq|\mathbf{p}_{oracle}|,\forall\mathbf{p}\in\mathcal{P}(f_{\theta},g,\mathbf{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, <em id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">i.e.</em> among all feasible paths, the optimal path requires the fewest sampling steps, while the oracle path requires the most sampling steps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Sampling Path and Oracle Path) ‣ 3.2 Free Draft-and-Verification Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2 (Feasible Path, Feasible Space, and Optimal Path) ‣ 3.2 Free Draft-and-Verification Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> indicate the great potential of DLLMs for lossless parallel decoding.
However, except for the oracle path <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{oracle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{oracle}</annotation></semantics></math>, all of the other feasible paths are agnostic to us.
We don’t know which steps can be merged into one step. Empirically setting a fixed number of transferred tokens or a fixed confidence threshold for parallel decoding is not guaranteed to get a feasible path that generates the same sequence as sampling via the oracle path, and the experimental results from both <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. [17]</a></cite> and us demonstrate that threshold-based parallel decoding is very likely to result in a non-negligible performance degradation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Verification-based Feasible Path Search)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the feasible space <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(f_{\theta},g,\mathbf{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐓</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(f_{\theta},g,\mathbf{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose we have a verifier function <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> defined as</span></p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(t_{n},d)=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if}~d=1\\
\min\{i|\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+i+1}}\neq\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+i}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+i}\rightarrow t_{n+i+1}},i=1,\dots,d-1\}&amp;\text{if}~d\geq 2\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(t_{n},d)=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if}~d=1\\
\min\{i|\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+i+1}}\neq\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+i}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+i}\rightarrow t_{n+i+1}},i=1,\dots,d-1\}&amp;\text{if}~d\geq 2\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a timestep and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive integer.
Then we can find a feasible path <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{0}}\rightarrow t_{a_{1}}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{M-1}}\rightarrow t_{a_{M}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{0}}\rightarrow t_{a_{1}}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{a_{M-1}}\rightarrow t_{a_{M}}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{M}=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{M}=N</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=h(t_{a_{i-1}},d),i\in\{1,\dots,M-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=h(t_{a_{i-1}},d),i\in\{1,\dots,M-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The verifier function defined in Equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="In Theorem 1 (Verification-based Feasible Path Search) ‣ 3.2 Free Draft-and-Verification Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> searches the maximum timestep from <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t_{n:n+d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n:n+d}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that the decision from <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> directly to this timestep is equal to the accumulation of decisions from the oracle path during the same time period.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq\|\mathbf{p}^{\star}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq\|\mathbf{p}^{\star}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> where
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}^{\star}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{a^{\star}_{0}}\rightarrow t_{a^{\star}_{1}}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{a^{\star}_{M-1}}\rightarrow t_{a^{\star}_{M}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}^{\star}=[\mathcal{I}_{t_{a^{\star}_{0}}\rightarrow t_{a^{\star}_{1}}},\dots,\mathcal{I}_{t_{a^{\star}_{M-1}}\rightarrow t_{a^{\star}_{M}}}]</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal path, and
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\mathbf{p}^{\star}\|_{\infty}=\max\{a^{\star}_{i+1}-a^{\star}_{i}|i=0,\dots,|\mathbf{p}^{\star}|-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{p}^{\star}\|_{\infty}=\max\{a^{\star}_{i+1}-a^{\star}_{i}|i=0,\dots,|\mathbf{p}^{\star}|-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
then <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\star}_{i}=h(t_{a^{\star}_{i-1}},d),i\in\{1,\dots,M-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\star}_{i}=h(t_{a^{\star}_{i-1}},d),i\in\{1,\dots,M-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof Sketch</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of this theorem is quite intuitive. Starting from any <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we find just the oracle path, which is also a feasible path; if <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, then from Equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="In Theorem 1 (Verification-based Feasible Path Search) ‣ 3.2 Free Draft-and-Verification Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> we have
<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+i+1}}=\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+i}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+i}\rightarrow t_{n+i+1}}\forall i\in\{1,\dots,h(t_{n},d)-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+i+1}}=\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+i}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+i}\rightarrow t_{n+i+1}}\forall i\in\{1,\dots,h(t_{n},d)-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, we have <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+2}}=\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+1}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+1}\rightarrow t_{n+2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+2}}=\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+1}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+1}\rightarrow t_{n+2}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+3}}=\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+2}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+2}\rightarrow t_{n+3}}=\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+1}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+1}\rightarrow t_{n+2}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+2}\rightarrow t_{n+3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+3}}=\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+2}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+2}\rightarrow t_{n+3}}=\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+1}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+1}\rightarrow t_{n+2}}\cup\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+2}\rightarrow t_{n+3}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dots</annotation></semantics></math>,
and recursively, we get
<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+h(t_{n},d)}}=\bigcup_{i=1}^{h(t_{n},d)-1}\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+i}\rightarrow t_{n+i+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t_{n}\rightarrow t_{n+h(t_{n},d)}}=\bigcup_{i=1}^{h(t_{n},d)-1}\mathcal{I}_{t_{n+i}\rightarrow t_{n+i+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which by Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2 (Feasible Path, Feasible Space, and Optimal Path) ‣ 3.2 Free Draft-and-Verification Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> induces a feasible path.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a verifier <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying Equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="In Theorem 1 (Verification-based Feasible Path Search) ‣ 3.2 Free Draft-and-Verification Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Verification-based Feasible Path Search) ‣ 3.2 Free Draft-and-Verification Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> provides the guarantee of searching a lossless, shorter (or equal) sampling path, and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 ‣ Remark ‣ 3.2 Free Draft-and-Verification Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> indicates the condition of finding the optimal path, <em id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.</em> <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> should be large enough to cover the size of the largest decision set in the optimal path. As <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is agnostic to us, we can find the sequence length as an upper bound such that <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\geq\|\mathbf{p}^{\star}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\geq\|\mathbf{p}^{\star}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>. As long as <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq L</annotation></semantics></math>, we are guaranteed to find the optimal path.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Based on our theoretical analysis above, we propose Free Draft-and-Verification (FreeDave), a fast sampling algorithm explicitly designed for DLLMs. Specifically, as shown in Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Proof Sketch ‣ 3.2 Free Draft-and-Verification Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Free Draft-and-Verification: Toward Lossless Parallel Decoding for Diffusion Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, FreeDave iteratively utilizes the remasking scheduler to sample draft candidates with different parallel decoding steps based on the estimated distribution predicted by the DLLM at the current step, and further verifies those candidates by the DLLM itself in the next step.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> DLLM FreeDave Sampling</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              Model <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, remasking scheduler <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, total generation length <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, total sampling steps <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, draft steps <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, time schedule array <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{T}=\{t_{0},\dots,t_{N}|1=t_{0}&gt;t_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;t_{N-1}&gt;t_{N}=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐓</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{T}=\{t_{0},\dots,t_{N}|1=t_{0}&gt;t_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;t_{N-1}&gt;t_{N}=0\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              The generated sequence <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{t_{0}}\leftarrow\textbf{m}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">m</mtext><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{0}}\leftarrow\textbf{m}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}_{0}\leftarrow f_{\theta}(x_{t_{0}},t_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}_{0}\leftarrow f_{\theta}(x_{t_{0}},t_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> initialize sequence and its estimated distribution
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\leftarrow\min(d,N-i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\leftarrow\min(d,N-i)</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> clip initial draft steps when no enough steps left
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{draft}\leftarrow[~]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{draft}\leftarrow[~]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1:d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1:d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
